  "notes": [
    "Release-wide inputs apply to every target; a target's keys override them (its pins are merged).",
    "web_build_time: WLED's UI build stamps WEB_BUILD_TIME (tools/cdata.js). The vendor reuses its build tree, so the UI was last generated at the original 16.0.1 release (2026-07-08). Read from a device's HTTP ETag; `discover.py stamp-at` finds it from any build with the same layout.",
    "PowerManager: v1.3.0, the newest tag before the images were built; the override fetches the default branch unpinned.",
    "QuickESPNow: WLED fetches the optional-debug branch, unpinned. PlatformIO caches it per env in the vendor's build tree, so the commit differs per target: the envs that existed in July 2026 have 193e991 (2025-03-17, release-wide pin); the V4 boards, added 2026-10-27, have 2985a4a (2026-09-27), which adds 152 bytes of code.",
    "checkout.autocrlf=false: the vendor's checkout had LF line endings; with Git for Windows' default (true), wled00/data/iro.js grows by 4 bytes inside the image.",
    "gzip_os=10: the vendor built on Windows, where Node writes OS byte 10 into the web UI's gzip headers.",
    "verified: per toolchain host. normalized_sha256 is the image with its ELF hash zeroed (imgdiff.normalized), which doesn't depend on build paths. On Windows it equals the vendor image's; Linux toolchains generate slightly different code.",
    "app_slot_bytes (dig-next-2): QuinLED's installer image for this board carries a 4 MB-style partition table even on its 8 MB flash (app0/app1 at 0x180000 each); an OTA image must fit one slot. The gate keeps 64 KiB free. Not yet checked for the other boards."
  ]
}
